# jubiku Qwen3.8-27B on the B70 (which also drives the desktop). Read by qwen27-jubiku.service.
# Hot load: the process stays up, but the engine unloads after QWEN_IDLE_UNLOAD s idle (VRAM back to the desktop)
# and the next request reloads it (about 28 s). Kept prompt states are lost at an unload.
# MLX 4/64 (orcarouter Uncensored): window 37 ms flat to 16 rows (EXL3 was 49 to 82).
# p36 build: embeddings on the host (XPU_EMBED_HOST, saves 0.72 GB). One shared pool of 245760 tokens int8 (8.18 GB),
# 2 streams of 114688. DFlash2 trees for a lone stream, chains when both streams run.
# XPU_KEEP_SHARED=1: kept prompt states share pool pages with the live stream, so a turn resumes at any length.
# Loaded, the server holds 25.2 to 25.9 GiB of 30.3 GiB. The desktop measured about 2 GiB.
# Measured 2026-11-02 MLX: DFlash2 95-126 tok/s code, 68-78 prose, 49 code at 39k; 180k prefill 877 tok/s, turn 2 resumes in 0.3 s.
# 2026-11-03: back to 1 stream x 217088 (Tim wants the long window). Pool 245760, 2-stream config: qwen27.env.bak-2x114k.
QWEN_BIN=/home/tlewis/b70/qwen27/bin/tensorfold-native-c664084e-fleet-tp1-skx
QWEN_MODEL=/home/tlewis/models/qwen38-27b/Qwen3.8-27B-Uncensored-MLX-4bit
QWEN_NAME=Qwen3.8-27B-Uncen-Jubiku
QWEN_CONTEXT=217088
QWEN_POOL_TOKENS=245760
QWEN_PORT=18197
XPU_MTP=0
XPU_KV_POOL=1
XPU_EMBED_HOST=1
# 2026-11-10 phase 1 window 3: prompt chunk 1024 rows (the engine default and the inference1 value), was 896.
# A cold prompt is 3.4 to 4.5% shorter: 31.1 s at 48k, 76.0 s at 100k, 133.8 s at 151k. Needles at 151k pass.
XPU_CHUNK=1024
QWEN_DRAFTER=/home/tlewis/models/qwen38-27b/Qwen3.8-27B-DFlash2
QWEN_IDLE_UNLOAD=300
XPU_KEEP_SHARED=1
QWEN_PARALLEL=1
# 2026-11-03: p39 138de4f4, K1 decode attention with DFlash2 chains (XPU_TREE=0). Exact sha at 120k. 142 tok/s short, 122 at 39k, 91.5 at 120k. p36 config: qwen27.env.bak-p36.
XPU_K1=1
# 2026-11-03: p42 7d08c424 (p39 K1 + reply fit). TF_REPLY_FLOOR=1 cuts max_tokens to the room left; the engine keeps 17 drafter slots, so a full-window reply is cut 17 short, never a 500.
TF_REPLY_FLOOR=1
QWEN_LOOP_GUARD=1
# 2026-11-10 phase 1: no page-fault mode in the Level Zero driver. With it the desktop render jobs suspend the
# compute queue and the GuC can reset the engine (Intel-B70-Recipe lanes/qwen27/receipts/p1-jubiku-window-1.md).
NEOReadDebugKeys=1
EnableRecoverablePageFaults=0
# 2026-11-10 phase 1 window 2: binary 690e93f6 (fork lane/fleet-serve). Chains ran it with XPU_DRAFT_WIN=512 from
# 08:14Z to 11:36Z (+4.7% on the mean of 7 thinking runs). Receipt: Intel-B70-Recipe
# lanes/qwen27/receipts/p1-jubiku-window-2.md. Rollback to the old binary: qwen27.env.bak-p1w2-20261110.
# 2026-11-10 phase 1 window 3 (Tim: enable the draft tree): XPU_TREE=0 removed, so a round drafts a DFlash2 tree,
# and XPU_K1_TREE=1 runs the tree windows on K1. The tree needs the full drafter window, so XPU_DRAFT_WIN is not
# set: 64.0 and 64.9 tok/s on the mean of 7 thinking runs. A 512 or 1024 window gave 62.2 to 64.1, chains with the
# 512 window 61.7, the config before phase 1 58.9.
# Known fault: the greedy eval is 38 to 40 of 41 against 40 for chains (the rows with the longest thinking run to
# the token cap in some starts), and the reply text changes from start to start.
# Receipt: Intel-B70-Recipe lanes/qwen27/receipts/p1-jubiku-window-3.md.
# Rollback to chains with the 512 window: qwen27.env.bak-p1w3-20261110.
XPU_K1_TREE=1
# 2026-11-12 phase 4 one-card (binary ab047651, fork lane/jubiku-p4, receipt Intel-B70-Recipe
# lanes/qwen27/receipts/jubiku-p4-1.md): XPU_GDN=103 (GS1 commit in one launch) and XPU_SMALLK=67.
# Window: ruler L mean +15.2% against the live set, 100k +6.9%, needles 3/3, eval 39/41, 0 xe lines.
# XPU_MV is left out: its picks are tuned for half-width ranks and ran -51% at 100k on this card.
XPU_GDN=103
XPU_SMALLK=67
# 2026-11-12 fleet-unified window (receipt Intel-B70-Recipe lanes/qwen27/receipts/jubiku-unify-1.md):
# switched to the fleet binary c664084e by lead decision. The window showed no loss.
# XPU_K1B=36 measured -1.6% at 100k against the no-K1B build and stays out.
